WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.203
- I have every reason
to be mad at the world.

00:00:05.573 --> 00:00:06.953
But I have an excuse.

00:00:07.842 --> 00:00:09.821
I have an excuse to be mad
at the world and everything,

00:00:09.821 --> 00:00:12.010
'cause of this right here, but I don't.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.387
I could give up, I'm not giving up.

00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:17.446
I can't give up.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.417
My mind and heart won't let me.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.320
- [Mark] All right, Jerry.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.040
We did a nice little talk last time,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.440
but I'd like to do the same,

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.490
kinda cover your whole
story from start to finish.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.260
And we'll just do a little
more comprehensive talk

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.660
than we did last time.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.047
So, before you were shot--

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.240
What year were you shot?

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.300
What year was it?

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.313
- Ooh man, okay, let me see.

00:00:52.326 --> 00:00:54.130
When was it?

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.995
I think I was about 42 or 43 years,

00:00:55.995 --> 00:00:57.033
it was about 42 years, I think.

00:00:57.969 --> 00:00:59.273
Was I 42?

00:00:59.273 --> 00:01:01.210
- [Mark] So like 13, 14, years ago?

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:02.670
- Something like that, probably.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:03.503
- [Mark] Yeah, so it's been a while.

00:01:03.503 --> 00:01:04.700
- Well, yeah.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.063
- [Mark] And what were
you doing before then?

00:01:07.063 --> 00:01:09.010
You had a full time job?

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.043
- I was a machinist.

00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:11.283
- [Mark] Machinist?

00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:12.380
- I made airplane parts.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.213
- [Mark] Airplane parts,

00:01:13.213 --> 00:01:15.410
and you were married,
single, do you have kids?

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.910
- Single.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.743
Kids, no.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:18.923
- [Mark] No kids, okay.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.630
And were you ever into drugs, or gangs,

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:24.530
or anything like that?

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.367
- No, no, definitely not,
I used to play sports.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.250
- [Mark] You used to be an athlete?

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.567
- I was a basketball player.

00:01:31.781 --> 00:01:32.900
Have you ever heard of the magazine

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.613
called Street &amp; Smith's?

00:01:34.613 --> 00:01:35.446
- [Mark] What is it?

00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:38.100
- A magazine called Street &amp; Smith's.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.933
- [Mark] I don't know.

00:01:38.933 --> 00:01:41.521
- It's a sports magazine,
like Sports Illustrated.

00:01:41.521 --> 00:01:45.110
- [Mark] Okay.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.263
- My teacher, not my
teacher, my counselor,

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.093
said he was in line one time,

00:01:51.598 --> 00:01:54.467
and he sees the book was open,

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:56.253
and he sees Ganesha High School.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.310
That's the school I go to.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.412
At school, he's a counselor, my counselor.

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:04.837
So when he grabbed the
book, it had my name in it.

00:02:04.837 --> 00:02:06.780
They had me, I think I was--

00:02:08.232 --> 00:02:10.920
They had me in there as one
of the top 75 high school

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.478
basketball players in
the state of California.

00:02:12.478 --> 00:02:13.314
- [Mark] Is that right?

00:02:13.314 --> 00:02:16.060
- And one of the top
250 basketball players

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:17.865
in the United States.

00:02:17.865 --> 00:02:18.875
- [Mark] Wow.

00:02:18.875 --> 00:02:21.025
- Basketball's my thing,
I love basketball.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.400
- [Mark] So you're a great athlete.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.430
- Yeah, I started as a sophomore,

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.627
I played three years of varsity,

00:02:29.627 --> 00:02:30.927
10th, 11th and 12th grade.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.810
I walked in in ninth grade
and those guys didn't like me.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.970
- [Mark] Why is that?

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:41.970
- I was a sophomore,
and I was starting off

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.060
and they were seniors.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:43.914
- [Mark] Oh, you were--

00:02:43.914 --> 00:02:45.500
(laughs)
- Yeah, I had problems.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.522
- [Mark] You were good for your age.

00:02:46.522 --> 00:02:47.713
- I was mad at the coach,

00:02:47.713 --> 00:02:51.821
because I could've played
varsity my ninth grade year.

00:02:51.821 --> 00:02:54.787
And he told me that it may be a problem.

00:02:54.787 --> 00:02:56.670
And my next year, it was a problem.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.077
Guys didn't like me
'cause I was a sophomore

00:02:59.077 --> 00:03:01.590
and everybody else was seniors.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.443
I was starting over
them, played more time.

00:03:03.443 --> 00:03:04.526
- [Mark] Wow.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.310
So when you were shot,
you were going to work?

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.247
You were coming home from work?

00:03:10.247 --> 00:03:11.152
- Coming home from work.

00:03:11.152 --> 00:03:12.930
- [Mark] Coming home from
work, and standing where?

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:13.763
- At a bus stop.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.990
- [Mark] And what happened?

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.038
- The next thing I know,
I woke up in the hospital,

00:03:18.038 --> 00:03:19.288
I thought I was dreaming.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.630
The doctor told me what happened to me.

00:03:26.054 --> 00:03:27.850
He said that he couldn't
believe I survived,

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.955
but he said the only reason I did survive,

00:03:29.955 --> 00:03:32.480
was because it was point blank range.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.494
He said if it wasn't point blank range,

00:03:34.494 --> 00:03:36.539
your head would have been
rolled down the streets.

00:03:36.539 --> 00:03:37.622
- [Mark] Wow.

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:41.740
- And the skin up here came off my leg.

00:03:43.587 --> 00:03:45.504
I have impaired vision.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.011
- [Mark] It's a skin graft?

00:03:48.011 --> 00:03:50.076
- Yeah, a skin graft, the
skin they took from my leg,

00:03:50.076 --> 00:03:51.893
they put up here.

00:03:51.893 --> 00:03:53.850
And this eye got a scar behind it,

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.470
it's making my vision messed up,

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.650
that's why the glasses won't help.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.984
- [Mark] So, you lost one eye?

00:03:58.984 --> 00:03:59.817
- Yeah.

00:03:59.817 --> 00:04:00.650
- [Mark] And your other eye?

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:01.920
- Yeah, impaired vision, blind, yeah.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.010
I had laser surgery and
everything, it did no good.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.053
I cannot breathe, or smell out my nose.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:11.740
- [Mark] Can you taste?

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:12.573
- Yeah, I can taste, yeah.

00:04:12.573 --> 00:04:14.246
- [Mark] You can taste.

00:04:14.246 --> 00:04:16.127
- I used to love to read,
but I can't read no more.

00:04:16.127 --> 00:04:17.220
- [Mark] You can't read,
'cause your vision's-

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.420
- Yeah.
- Impaired now.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.613
So how long were you in the hospital?

00:04:24.579 --> 00:04:27.783
- I was there for a
while, man, yeah, yeah.

00:04:27.783 --> 00:04:30.540
Then I left the hospital,

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.823
I had to go to Rancho Los Amigos,

00:04:34.029 --> 00:04:35.074
you remember that?

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:35.907
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:04:35.907 --> 00:04:39.097
- Rancho Los Amigos, I was
there, off the Imperial.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.190
A rehabilitation center.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:42.118
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:04:42.118 --> 00:04:44.359
- Rancho Cucamonga, something like that.

00:04:44.359 --> 00:04:46.693
Off Imperial, yeah, I
was there for a while.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.890
- [Mark] So the surgery
must have been incredible.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.033
- They said 22 hour surgery.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.080
I had surgery on my arm too.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.304
They took a vein out my leg,

00:04:57.304 --> 00:04:59.162
and put it in this arm right here.

00:04:59.162 --> 00:04:59.995
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:04:59.995 --> 00:05:02.354
- They took a vein out of one of my legs,

00:05:02.354 --> 00:05:03.539
and put it in this arm right here.

00:05:03.539 --> 00:05:04.433
- [Mark] Oh, they put a vein.

00:05:04.433 --> 00:05:07.811
- You've seen this arm
before, haven't you?

00:05:07.811 --> 00:05:08.644
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:05:08.644 --> 00:05:09.477
- You've seen my arm, haven't you?

00:05:09.477 --> 00:05:10.632
- [Mark] I've never seen your arm.

00:05:10.632 --> 00:05:11.465
- You haven't seen this thing?

00:05:11.465 --> 00:05:13.125
- [Mark] You always have a sock over it.

00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:14.625
- Let me show you.

00:05:16.831 --> 00:05:19.081
(grunting)

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.200
I got shot here too, in my arm.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.450
(grunting)

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:39.576
Another minute.

00:05:39.576 --> 00:05:40.409
You see this right here?

00:05:40.409 --> 00:05:41.492
- [Mark] Yeah, I see the scar.

00:05:41.492 --> 00:05:42.742
- You see that?

00:05:44.916 --> 00:05:47.166
I can't move it, that's
all I can do is this.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.408
It swells up.

00:05:50.408 --> 00:05:52.347
- [Mark] So what did they do to your hand?

00:05:52.347 --> 00:05:53.903
- I got shot in the elbow.

00:05:53.903 --> 00:05:54.773
- [Mark] Can you hold that?

00:05:54.773 --> 00:05:57.023
(mumbling)

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.990
(grunting)

00:06:05.035 --> 00:06:05.871
- [Mark] Want me to help you?

00:06:05.871 --> 00:06:08.228
- It's happening, i'll get it out again.

00:06:08.228 --> 00:06:09.395
- [Mark] Here.

00:06:10.585 --> 00:06:13.020
(grunting)

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.423
- [Mark] Let me help you.

00:06:15.423 --> 00:06:16.421
Why don't you take your jacket off, too?

00:06:16.421 --> 00:06:18.197
- No, I don't want to take it off.

00:06:18.197 --> 00:06:19.280
Look at that.

00:06:22.085 --> 00:06:23.298
There we go, you got it.
- There we go.

00:06:23.298 --> 00:06:26.215
- All right, you see all this here?

00:06:27.648 --> 00:06:29.030
This is as far as I can bring my arm down,

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.065
where you at, over here.

00:06:30.065 --> 00:06:30.898
- [Mark] Right here.

00:06:30.898 --> 00:06:31.731
- You see my arm like this?

00:06:31.731 --> 00:06:32.564
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:32.564 --> 00:06:33.485
- I can't straighten it out.

00:06:33.485 --> 00:06:34.403
- [Mark] Oh, you can't straighten it?

00:06:34.403 --> 00:06:36.988
- No I can't, listen to this.

00:06:36.988 --> 00:06:39.330
As long as it's hanging down like this,

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.280
ooh, it was a pain!

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.860
I kept it in a sling, right?

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:47.100
And the doctor told me,
Jerry, take the pain,

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.532
do not let your hand
in the sling like that,

00:06:50.532 --> 00:06:51.368
you'll mess it up.

00:06:51.368 --> 00:06:52.370
And then listen what he says then.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.407
If I had my hand in my sling,

00:06:53.407 --> 00:06:56.367
and I hold it like this all the time,

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:57.767
my arm would stay like this.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:06:59.820
That's why he was telling me,

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:02.576
keep it out of that
sling, just take the pain.

00:07:02.576 --> 00:07:05.455
They wanted to break it
to straighten it out.

00:07:05.455 --> 00:07:06.630
And they took the veins
out of one of these legs,

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.780
to put it in this arm right here.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.304
The bone was sticking out.

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:11.605
- [Mark] Oh, jeez.

00:07:11.605 --> 00:07:13.457
- That was what did this to it.

00:07:13.457 --> 00:07:14.973
- [Mark] So, your hand
was shot, or your arm?

00:07:14.973 --> 00:07:16.800
- No, it was the elbow.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.633
- [Mark] The elbow was shot?

00:07:17.633 --> 00:07:19.213
- Elbow right here.

00:07:19.213 --> 00:07:20.530
- [Mark] Were you right-handed?

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:21.363
- Luckily, I was left-handed.

00:07:21.363 --> 00:07:23.410
It was softball, more in softball, yeah.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.354
- [Mark] You're left-handed?

00:07:24.354 --> 00:07:25.187
- Yeah, I'm left-handed, yeah.

00:07:25.187 --> 00:07:26.785
- [Mark] Oh, that's lucky.

00:07:26.785 --> 00:07:28.144
- Yeah.

00:07:28.144 --> 00:07:30.810
I used to love to read, I miss reading.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.180
I can't play basketball no more.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.370
- [Mark] No, you can't.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.393
- Yeah.

00:07:41.893 --> 00:07:43.990
I used to take the seizure pills.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:44.823
- [Mark] Yeah, you told me

00:07:44.823 --> 00:07:46.263
that you took seizure pills, medications.

00:07:47.808 --> 00:07:49.840
- This one doctor told me,

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.499
he said, Jerry, before the head injury,

00:07:53.499 --> 00:07:54.393
were you taking this kind of medication?

00:07:54.393 --> 00:07:55.461
I said no.

00:07:55.461 --> 00:07:56.534
This is just how he said it, he said,

00:07:56.534 --> 00:07:57.970
I don't know why the fuck
they gave you this shit.

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.380
It'll start making you have them.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:03.953
But not just seizures, I'd
have blackout seizures.

00:08:03.953 --> 00:08:06.879
I'm gonna tell you this story right here.

00:08:06.879 --> 00:08:08.237
It's a good one.

00:08:08.237 --> 00:08:11.412
I was at Kentucky Fried
Chicken one time, right?

00:08:11.412 --> 00:08:13.570
Last thing I remember,

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:17.060
I was standing in line
to buy some chicken.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.133
Then I woke up in the hospital
with these on my chest.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.130
I thought, what the hell's going on?

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:24.963
I went back to Kentucky Fried Chicken.

00:08:24.963 --> 00:08:27.203
The security guard said,
Jerry, you started tripping!

00:08:28.383 --> 00:08:29.614
He said, man, you were
trying to fight everybody.

00:08:29.614 --> 00:08:31.790
He said I jumped over the counter,

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:34.780
and grabbed all the chicken
and threw it everywhere.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.690
And then, I jumped back over,

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:39.743
I passed out and went into a seizure.

00:08:39.743 --> 00:08:43.110
Here's another story
right here, another one.

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:44.030
Before I was sitting there,

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:46.630
I used to sit down, have
you seen me on Hill Street?

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.013
- [Mark] No.

00:08:50.362 --> 00:08:53.311
- On Hill and First Street
is the court building there.

00:08:53.311 --> 00:08:54.144
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:54.144 --> 00:08:54.977
- You know what I'm talking about?

00:08:54.977 --> 00:08:55.810
- [Mark] Yeah, I know the court building.

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:57.409
- It's over there.

00:08:57.409 --> 00:08:58.624
There was a deputy that
used to come down there,

00:08:58.624 --> 00:09:00.780
the sheriff deputy.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:04.402
We really liked each other,
and we became friends, right?

00:09:04.402 --> 00:09:05.447
We were real good friends and everything.

00:09:05.447 --> 00:09:07.957
Yeah, it's cool, you go ahead
and stay there, you know.

00:09:09.703 --> 00:09:12.713
One time, everybody
said, you gotta get up.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:18.090
I was laying next to
the Los Angeles Times.

00:09:19.056 --> 00:09:22.123
Somebody took my tennis shoes, my shoes.

00:09:22.123 --> 00:09:23.580
My head was bleeding down here,

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.287
right here, bleeding real bad.

00:09:26.287 --> 00:09:27.274
I wondered what happened to me,

00:09:27.274 --> 00:09:29.178
I must have had a blackout
seizure or something like that,

00:09:29.178 --> 00:09:30.339
what happened to me?

00:09:30.339 --> 00:09:33.691
And I wondered what happened to me, yeah.

00:09:33.691 --> 00:09:34.527
That deputy I was telling you about,

00:09:34.527 --> 00:09:36.862
that sheriff's deputy I
was telling you about?

00:09:36.862 --> 00:09:39.270
(mumbles)

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:40.940
He came over to where I was sleeping at.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.991
He said, Jerry, what the
fuck was wrong with you, man?

00:09:43.991 --> 00:09:46.039
I said, What are you talking about?

00:09:46.039 --> 00:09:50.610
He said, I seen you, blood was
running all down your face.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.307
He said, I called an ambulance for you,

00:09:52.307 --> 00:09:53.490
and you tried to fight them,

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.729
and you scared them to death.

00:09:54.729 --> 00:09:56.083
You guys know what he told me?

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:59.100
He said, you tried to take my gun from me.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.532
You were wrestling me over my
gun, and you slipped and fell.

00:10:01.532 --> 00:10:02.920
That's how I got control over it.

00:10:03.761 --> 00:10:05.370
I didn't know that.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.407
- [Mark] This was the seizure medication?

00:10:07.407 --> 00:10:09.090
- Yeah that it, now yeah.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:10.940
I knew him, see?

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.620
He said blood, I don't
know if you can see,

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.510
there's a cut right there.

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:14.706
- [Mark] Yeah, I see it.

00:10:14.706 --> 00:10:16.360
- It was wide open.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.701
He said, when I seen you, man,

00:10:17.701 --> 00:10:19.994
you had blood like a faucet
running down your face.

00:10:19.994 --> 00:10:22.160
He called the ambulance, he said,

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.138
you scared them away,
you tried to fight them,

00:10:24.138 --> 00:10:24.971
and then he said, you grabbed my gun

00:10:24.971 --> 00:10:27.745
straight out the holster and
man, you was wrestling over it,

00:10:27.745 --> 00:10:28.674
and then you slipped and fell,

00:10:28.674 --> 00:10:30.427
and that's how I got control of my gun.

00:10:30.427 --> 00:10:31.449
I don't remember any of that,

00:10:31.449 --> 00:10:35.489
but if he didn't know me,
he could have killed me.

00:10:35.489 --> 00:10:38.156
I said, you've got to be joking.

00:10:39.398 --> 00:10:42.776
The doctor told me I've got
to stop taking that stuff.

00:10:42.776 --> 00:10:46.039
The medication is doing that,
you don't remember nothing.

00:10:46.039 --> 00:10:48.140
It was real bad, yes I'm
glad, I'm glad me know me,

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:51.890
'cause if not, when he
first got over there--

00:10:53.242 --> 00:10:56.655
Are you by yourself, you
gotta be by yourself.

00:10:56.655 --> 00:10:58.014
If you were somebody else,

00:10:58.014 --> 00:11:00.012
and you were wrestling
me for my gun like that?

00:11:00.012 --> 00:11:01.904
He could have shot and killed me.

00:11:01.904 --> 00:11:05.283
I was wondering what happened,
too, I said, what happened?

00:11:05.283 --> 00:11:07.732
I don't know how I got this scar,

00:11:07.732 --> 00:11:09.033
and got my bleeding like that

00:11:09.033 --> 00:11:11.761
I don't remember, you see,
you don't remember nothing.

00:11:11.761 --> 00:11:12.620
- [Mark] Yeah, you don't remember it.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.787
- I don't remember none of that stuff.

00:11:18.924 --> 00:11:23.330
And then, one time, it was
because of my sight thing.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.997
Okay, I was walking,

00:11:26.871 --> 00:11:30.911
I told you about my eye, my
vision thing with my eye, right?

00:11:30.911 --> 00:11:32.494
I was walking down,

00:11:34.255 --> 00:11:36.669
let me see, this street right here.

00:11:36.669 --> 00:11:37.502
- [Mark] Seventh?

00:11:37.502 --> 00:11:40.669
- Yeah, I'm going to Central, went up.

00:11:43.032 --> 00:11:44.808
There's a gas station right there,

00:11:44.808 --> 00:11:45.853
before you get to the freeway, right?

00:11:45.853 --> 00:11:46.686
- [Mark] Mmhmm.

00:11:46.686 --> 00:11:49.178
- All the way that way, I'm walking.

00:11:49.178 --> 00:11:52.255
I said, man this side of the
street's narrow over here.

00:11:52.255 --> 00:11:54.600
I'm going down the street
to cut down this way.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.211
I said, damn, man, these
cars driving right here

00:11:56.211 --> 00:11:57.151
like they're crazy!

00:11:57.151 --> 00:11:59.601
There's something wrong with them.

00:11:59.601 --> 00:12:01.725
I said, I'm gonna cross the
street to the other side.

00:12:01.725 --> 00:12:05.336
I go across the street, damn
there's no sidewalk over here!

00:12:05.336 --> 00:12:07.666
So I go back, when I get back on it,

00:12:07.666 --> 00:12:09.628
they're driving clean on the side.

00:12:09.628 --> 00:12:11.711
Now check this out, Mark.

00:12:12.577 --> 00:12:14.417
You know why the cars were
driving on the side like that,

00:12:14.417 --> 00:12:16.483
and the sidewalk was narrow?

00:12:16.483 --> 00:12:20.192
I'm not doing that, I was
walking on the damn freeway!

00:12:20.192 --> 00:12:21.411
When I got back to the street I meant to,

00:12:21.411 --> 00:12:24.000
I seen it, and I said,
ain't this but a bitch?

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.083
What way to find out that
I was going back and forth

00:12:26.083 --> 00:12:27.964
across the street on the damn freeway.

00:12:27.964 --> 00:12:29.845
I thought I was on the street.

00:12:29.845 --> 00:12:31.528
I said no wonder the damn sidewalk was,

00:12:31.528 --> 00:12:34.570
the sidewalk was real narrow.

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:35.487
I was looking, and I seen houses.

00:12:35.487 --> 00:12:39.295
I said, why them houses way
back there from the sidewalk?

00:12:39.295 --> 00:12:40.352
And these sidewalks were real narrow.

00:12:40.352 --> 00:12:42.117
Now, I go on the other side of the street,

00:12:42.117 --> 00:12:44.903
man, they ain't got no sidewalk over here!

00:12:44.903 --> 00:12:45.860
And the cars were driving crazy,

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:50.562
and I'm walking on the
side, and I'm blind to it.

00:12:50.562 --> 00:12:52.395
And so, I was walking,

00:12:53.581 --> 00:12:58.248
right here, San Pedro right
here, that's where you exit.

00:12:59.583 --> 00:13:02.242
I saw the signs on the freeway to exit.

00:13:02.242 --> 00:13:03.762
I said, ain't this but a bitch!

00:13:03.762 --> 00:13:04.680
- [Mark] You were walking on the freeway.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.762
- I was walking on the freeway
and didn't even know it!

00:13:06.762 --> 00:13:08.140
I was walking back and
forth across the freeway,

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.190
cars are flying by, and I was thinking,

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:12.040
what the hell's wrong with
them, driving crazy like that?

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.170
- [Mark] You crossed the freeway?

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:14.443
- Yeah, that's what I'm saying.

00:13:14.443 --> 00:13:15.499
I walk on one side,

00:13:15.499 --> 00:13:18.077
where I said the sidewalk
was narrow, right?

00:13:18.077 --> 00:13:20.822
I said, why is the sidewalk
so narrow like this?

00:13:20.822 --> 00:13:23.666
And I was looking like, let
me walk on the other side.

00:13:23.666 --> 00:13:25.419
I walk over to the other side,

00:13:25.419 --> 00:13:28.287
damn, they ain't got no
sidewalk on this side!

00:13:28.287 --> 00:13:29.158
Cars were going.

00:13:29.158 --> 00:13:30.121
- [Mark] 'Cause your vision is so bad?

00:13:30.121 --> 00:13:32.687
- Right, I walk back to the other side.

00:13:32.687 --> 00:13:34.405
I'm walking.

00:13:34.405 --> 00:13:37.810
you know, on the freeway where it says,

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:39.800
exit 70 whatever, right?

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:40.890
I said, ain't this but a bitch!

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:44.140
I see a sign says, exit San Pedro.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.210
I said, ain't this but a bitch!

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.003
No wonder they were flying
down the street like that!

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:51.323
I was walking on the
freeway and did not know it.

00:13:51.323 --> 00:13:54.385
It was at nighttime,
not daytime, nighttime.

00:13:54.385 --> 00:13:56.872
I said, man, man, man, man.

00:13:56.872 --> 00:13:58.539
Another thing, man--

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.755
- [Mark] They never caught
the guy who shot you?

00:14:02.755 --> 00:14:03.670
- I don't know who did it.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:04.598
- [Mark] You don't know who did it?

00:14:04.598 --> 00:14:05.431
- Nuh uh.

00:14:05.431 --> 00:14:06.264
- [Mark] You never saw it coming?

00:14:06.264 --> 00:14:07.097
- Never seen nothing.

00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:08.316
- [Mark] They never caught the guy?

00:14:08.316 --> 00:14:09.825
- Last thing I remember,

00:14:09.825 --> 00:14:12.170
I was sitting like I'm
sitting right here, and pow!

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:13.993
I woke up, thought I was dreaming.

00:14:13.993 --> 00:14:16.199
I said, where the hell am I at?

00:14:16.199 --> 00:14:17.532
What's going on?

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.990
I didn't know I was in the hospital.

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:22.730
They said I had a 22 hour surgery.

00:14:27.689 --> 00:14:29.689
I mean, I was messed up.

00:14:30.569 --> 00:14:33.373
They didn't think I was going to make it.

00:14:33.373 --> 00:14:35.573
This one guy told me, I remember seeing.

00:14:35.573 --> 00:14:36.406
He see me,

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:38.777
he said, it is you.

00:14:38.777 --> 00:14:40.000
Yeah, who am I?

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.819
Mark, do you remember they
talked about some woman,

00:14:42.819 --> 00:14:47.068
where a monkey pulled her face
off or something like that?

00:14:47.068 --> 00:14:48.319
You recall that, you remember that?

00:14:48.319 --> 00:14:49.370
- [Mark] From a chimpanzee, right?

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.010
- Yeah.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:53.070
He said they've got you and that lady

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:55.023
in the medical mystery,

00:14:56.563 --> 00:14:58.773
medical history, medical books,

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:00.870
for y'all surviving
what happened to y'all.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.040
- [Mark] Yeah, they re-built your face.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:03.873
- Yeah.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:07.068
Yeah, okay, they said they got me

00:15:07.068 --> 00:15:12.068
in a medical history book for
surviving what happened to me.

00:15:16.808 --> 00:15:21.808
One guy told me he saw me on
a video game on the internet.

00:15:23.553 --> 00:15:25.760
And one guy showed me the cover of a CD

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:26.860
with my picture on it.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:28.623
Okay, so yeah.

00:15:30.798 --> 00:15:31.850
- [Mark] So do you have feelings of anger

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:34.595
towards the person that shot you?

00:15:34.595 --> 00:15:35.428
- No, not really, not really.

00:15:35.428 --> 00:15:37.320
I can't, I'm not gonna give them that.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.870
I heard about what happened
in the video, because I--

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.010
I still go through it.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:49.313
I never forget that, yeah.

00:15:49.313 --> 00:15:52.396
People look at me, I get rude people.

00:15:53.493 --> 00:15:54.893
Some people call me monster.

00:15:56.853 --> 00:15:57.686
And then you've got some

00:15:57.686 --> 00:16:02.686
lovely people out there too,
like yourself, yourself, yeah.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:05.270
I keep my faith in God, though.

00:16:08.068 --> 00:16:13.068
With God standing with you,
nobody can stand against you.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.800
- [Mark] Were you religious before you--

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.172
I hear you mention God a lot.

00:16:16.172 --> 00:16:17.005
- Yeah, yeah.

00:16:17.005 --> 00:16:18.140
- [Mark] Were you religious
before you were shot?

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:18.973
- Oh, definitely, yeah.

00:16:18.973 --> 00:16:19.850
- [Mark] You were?

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:22.580
- My mother kept us in church.

00:16:26.208 --> 00:16:27.853
The Bible says, there's
nothing new under the sun,

00:16:27.853 --> 00:16:29.525
the Bible says.

00:16:29.525 --> 00:16:31.777
Everything that's going
on right now, today,

00:16:31.777 --> 00:16:35.220
happened before in the Bible,
in the Bible, and before.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.060
Everything, everything, like I said,

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:38.360
nothing new under the sun.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.795
See, everything that happens
right now on this earth

00:16:41.795 --> 00:16:43.378
happened years ago.

00:16:45.715 --> 00:16:47.167
- [Mark] Do you have family?

00:16:47.167 --> 00:16:50.162
- [Jerry] I haven't seen
my family in a while.

00:16:50.162 --> 00:16:51.912
It's been awhile now.

00:16:56.318 --> 00:16:57.418
It's been a long time.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.537
I wish I could get in touch with them.

00:17:02.537 --> 00:17:04.487
They know where I'm at.

00:17:04.487 --> 00:17:05.860
- [Mark] They know where you are?

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:08.191
- [Jerry] If they want to find me, yeah.

00:17:08.191 --> 00:17:11.117
I only talk to my youngest brother.

00:17:11.117 --> 00:17:13.026
(mumbles)

00:17:13.026 --> 00:17:16.453
Where you see me at the ground
over at the flower district?

00:17:16.453 --> 00:17:17.370
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:19.953
- [Jerry] That's where I be at.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:23.996
- [Mark] Is your mom still alive?

00:17:23.996 --> 00:17:26.155
- [Jerry] Yes, well, I
think she is, I hope so.

00:17:26.155 --> 00:17:27.777
- [Mark] And she doesn't contact you?

00:17:27.777 --> 00:17:29.792
- [Jerry] Uh huh, I haven't talked to her.

00:17:29.792 --> 00:17:32.644
She don't, but my youngest brother do.

00:17:32.644 --> 00:17:33.680
- [Mark] Did you have
contact with your mom

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:34.640
before the accident?

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:37.113
- [Jerry] Before, and after, after, yeah.

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:38.963
- [Mark] But not lately?

00:17:38.963 --> 00:17:40.000
- [Jerry] Yeah, yeah.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.294
- [Mark] What's changed?

00:17:41.294 --> 00:17:42.457
- [Jerry] I used to, I
don't know, I used to--

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:50.454
- [Mark] And where was your dad?

00:17:50.454 --> 00:17:52.673
- [Jerry] My dad, somebody
told me he passed away.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:55.203
Recently too.

00:17:58.145 --> 00:17:59.403
When I was growing up as a child,

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:01.953
let me put it this way, Mark,

00:18:01.953 --> 00:18:03.555
so you'll understand.

00:18:03.555 --> 00:18:06.191
I've probably seen you more
times than I've seen my father.

00:18:06.191 --> 00:18:07.024
- [Mark] You've seen me more times

00:18:07.024 --> 00:18:08.172
than you've seen your father?
- Just about, yeah.

00:18:08.172 --> 00:18:09.051
- [Mark] Oh my god.

00:18:09.051 --> 00:18:12.070
- [Jerry] He was a construction worker.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:14.983
You know those twin towers
down there on Seventh Street?

00:18:15.906 --> 00:18:16.820
Where those twin towers at?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:17.653
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:18:17.653 --> 00:18:19.407
- He was the one who helped build them.

00:18:19.407 --> 00:18:20.240
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.273
- Yeah, he was a construction worker.

00:18:22.273 --> 00:18:25.015
I loved math, I guess I got that from him.

00:18:25.015 --> 00:18:28.147
He knew all that math really well.

00:18:28.147 --> 00:18:29.750
- [Mark] But he wasn't
really in your life?

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:31.027
- No, nuh uh.

00:18:31.027 --> 00:18:32.800
- [Mark] And your childhood was good?

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:33.633
- Yes, yeah.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:35.830
- [Mark] Nothing crazy went on?

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.980
- No, no, my mother kept us in line.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.430
- [Mark] Your mom kept
you in line, that's great.

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:43.945
- [Mark] You have any friends, Jerry?

00:18:43.945 --> 00:18:45.830
- I don't mess with anybody, no.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:46.663
- [Mark] No?

00:18:49.616 --> 00:18:51.966
- [Mark] What are your
thoughts on forgiveness?

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:56.570
- If you about to forgive?

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:59.793
Well this, in order to forgive,
you have to forget first.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.120
That's forgiveness, forget.

00:19:04.198 --> 00:19:06.032
If you can't forget, you can't forgive.

00:19:06.032 --> 00:19:07.932
Wouldn't you say so, isn't that right?

00:19:09.492 --> 00:19:10.742
What you think?

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:14.530
- [Mark] You forget
completely, you wash it clean?

00:19:15.796 --> 00:19:17.420
- If you want to forgive,
you've got to forget.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:19.070
You can't forgive without forgetting.

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:19.903
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:21.963
- Yeah, that's it.

00:19:21.963 --> 00:19:23.073
- [Mark] It never happened.

00:19:23.073 --> 00:19:25.900
- Like it never happened, yeah.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.030
- [Mark] If you're still
hanging onto the fact

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.780
that that happened, you're
not really forgiving.

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:31.163
- That's right.

00:19:31.163 --> 00:19:33.747
I don't know how I can say this.

00:19:37.011 --> 00:19:37.844
I'm not saying it the correct way,

00:19:37.844 --> 00:19:40.430
but this is what is says in the Bible.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:44.410
I can't remember the sentence right here.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:48.617
Change what you can, and
accept what you can't.

00:19:48.617 --> 00:19:50.080
Somewhere in the Bible it says that.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:50.927
- [Mark] Say it again?

00:19:50.927 --> 00:19:51.760
This is what it says in the Bible.

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:52.593
I'm not saying it the correct way,

00:19:52.593 --> 00:19:53.437
but I'm saying this is
what it says in the Bible.

00:19:54.949 --> 00:19:55.782
It says,

00:19:56.726 --> 00:19:57.559
change

00:19:58.820 --> 00:19:59.657
what you can,

00:20:01.776 --> 00:20:02.609
and...

00:20:04.737 --> 00:20:05.570
- [Mark] Accept.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.836
- Accept what you can't.

00:20:07.836 --> 00:20:08.911
- [Mark] What you can't.

00:20:08.911 --> 00:20:09.744
It says in the Bible something like that.

00:20:09.744 --> 00:20:14.297
It says, change what you can,
and accept what you can't.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:19.170
- [Mark] So Jerry, if
you could have anything

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.113
in the world, anything you
want, what would it be?

00:20:26.438 --> 00:20:27.638
- The world to be happy.

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:30.950
Happiness for everybody.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:33.313
No homeless.

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:37.537
Everybody be able to eat,
live, I mean, you have a great,

00:20:37.537 --> 00:20:39.975
you know what I'm saying?

00:20:39.975 --> 00:20:44.364
That would be the happiest
thing in the world.

00:20:44.364 --> 00:20:46.930
- [Mark] Nothing for you?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:47.905
- That would be for me.

00:20:47.905 --> 00:20:49.101
- [Mark] A nicer place to live?

00:20:49.101 --> 00:20:50.472
No, the whole world, a nicer
place for the whole world,

00:20:50.472 --> 00:20:52.389
just not me, everybody.

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:58.373
We'd all be happy, living in society.

00:21:02.198 --> 00:21:03.160
What you think?

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:04.960
- [Mark] Yeah, that's a beautiful,

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.276
that's the most beautiful answer
you could ever give, right?

00:21:07.276 --> 00:21:09.990
- Yeah, it is, yeah.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:11.550
- [Mark] You're an amazing guy, Jerry.

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:12.383
- Yeah.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.970
What you all been doing lately?

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:21.860
- [Mark] Wait, what?

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.651
- I gotta get me a radio,
that what I need is a radio.

00:21:23.651 --> 00:21:24.550
- [Mark] You need a radio?

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:25.383
- That's what I need, a radio.

00:21:25.383 --> 00:21:26.484
- [Mark] Let me go get you a radio.

00:21:26.484 --> 00:21:27.900
(mumbles)

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:28.733
- [Mark] That's the first time

00:21:28.733 --> 00:21:29.566
you've ever asked for anything.

00:21:29.566 --> 00:21:31.810
- I gotta keep up with--

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:32.657
- [Mark] I'm asking you
anything in the world,

00:21:32.657 --> 00:21:33.590
and you want a radio.

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:35.210
- Yeah, see I can't see TV.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:37.340
- [Mark] Okay, I'll get you a radio.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:38.673
I'll go get you one right now.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.420
I'm asking you if you want
something significant,

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:42.930
and you're just saying a radio.

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:44.980
So Jerry, do people ever give you,

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:47.130
like kids ever react to you
like they're scared of you,

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:47.963
or stuff like like?

00:21:47.963 --> 00:21:50.995
- Some love me, some
hate me, some will cry,

00:21:50.995 --> 00:21:53.162
even adults, adult people.

00:21:54.431 --> 00:21:55.520
- [Mark] What do they
think, that you're like

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:56.777
deformed, or what do they think?

00:21:56.777 --> 00:21:58.300
- A lot of them think
I was born like this.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.389
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:21:59.389 --> 00:22:02.500
- Some will be like, you have a twin?

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.333
A twin.

00:22:04.573 --> 00:22:05.980
They don't know.

00:22:05.980 --> 00:22:07.000
- [Mark] Oh, I see, like they separated.

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:08.738
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:22:08.738 --> 00:22:10.410
Like I said, some people sit by me,

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:11.662
(mumbles)

00:22:11.662 --> 00:22:12.750
laugh with me.

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:14.865
Those kids are something else, though.

00:22:14.865 --> 00:22:16.132
They got a mind of their own.

00:22:16.132 --> 00:22:18.048
(laughs)

00:22:18.048 --> 00:22:22.216
One guy told me, hey, you
gonna be here for a while?

00:22:22.216 --> 00:22:23.830
I said, yeah.

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:24.840
I said, why?

00:22:24.840 --> 00:22:27.928
I got crystal, I've
been saving up my money.

00:22:27.928 --> 00:22:29.867
His friend, who he brought to me,

00:22:29.867 --> 00:22:33.200
said he was gonna bring me this crystal.

00:22:34.778 --> 00:22:35.960
He had a crystal in a bag,

00:22:35.960 --> 00:22:37.871
I guess a crystal that's
worth a lot of money.

00:22:37.871 --> 00:22:38.905
(laughs)

00:22:38.905 --> 00:22:41.240
Boy, kids are something else, boy,

00:22:41.240 --> 00:22:43.340
man, they're so beautiful!

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:47.320
You've got some that are scared, they cry.

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:50.053
And I have people call me
names, the whole thing.

00:22:53.069 --> 00:22:53.902
But I love life, though, man.

00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:01.903
- [Mark] What's your view of the world?

00:23:01.903 --> 00:23:04.060
Do you see the world as a
mean place, cruel place,

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:05.393
or a loving place?

00:23:07.488 --> 00:23:08.710
- It can be a loving place.

00:23:08.710 --> 00:23:09.610
Right, I gotta say

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:12.920
life is just about what you make it.

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:17.273
So, in a way, and again,

00:23:18.880 --> 00:23:21.233
it can be people that's holding you back.

00:23:23.020 --> 00:23:28.020
They don't want to see you make it.

00:23:28.161 --> 00:23:29.206
Like I said, if you keep God in your life,

00:23:29.206 --> 00:23:31.250
it's just a loving place.

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:32.329
It's a very loving place.

00:23:32.329 --> 00:23:34.493
If you have trust in
God, it's a loving place.

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:37.143
Definitely.

00:23:42.010 --> 00:23:45.750
I just want the world to be
living as one, and be happy.

00:23:46.864 --> 00:23:48.343
If the world could live
as one, and be happy,

00:23:48.343 --> 00:23:52.913
I mean everyone, Russia, the
whole world, living as one.

00:23:57.078 --> 00:23:59.495
One day it might be that way.

00:24:18.289 --> 00:24:21.122
(coins jingling)

